  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Friday...\n\nCurrent upper level pattern showers troughing moving into Idaho\nand western MT, bringing small (10-30%) chances for precipitation\nacross the higher terrain of south central MT. Meanwhile, low\nstratus is attempting to lift along the MT/Dakotas border late \nthis morning. With a modest pressure gradient remaining over \nsoutheast MT, breezy conditions will remain in place with \nsoutheast wind gusts of 20-30 mph. As a more southwest flow builds\nin aloft, a weak pressure gradient favorable breezy conditions \nfor the Livingston/Big Timber/Nye areas this evening and through \nthe day Sunday. Wind gusts 30-45 mph are expected with about a 40%\nchance for a gust to at least 50 mph. There is also a small chance\n(20%) for fog across southeast MT again tonight into Sunday \nmorning, mainly across the river valleys. Tuesday into Wednesday, \nensembles continue to show shortwave troughing moving through the \nregion, but is more consistently showing splitting energy as the \nwave approaches. This in turn has decreased precipitation amounts \nand lessened the amount of cool air. There is confidence in cooler\nand wetter conditions, but uncertainty to what extent. An \nadditional system following this wave looks to move in towards the\nend of the week continuing this trend. Temperatures look to \nremain in the 40s and 50s through mid week, potentially cooling \ninto the upper 30s and 40s for the latter half of week. TS",
